<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on May 15.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on May 15.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Jilin		  SLD May 07	 11,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Alam Tenaga	  SLD May 11	 15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangbunnak	   SLD May 09	  5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Jin Cheng Jiang    SLD May 08	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Naftilos	     SLD May 11	 18,000	Japan</p>
<p>Tolich		 SLD May 07	 12,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Bangramad	    SLD May 12	  5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Yick Zao	     SLD May 10	 29,400	S.Korea</p>
<p>Kapitan Dublitskiy SLD May 08	  9,500	S.Korea</p>
<p>Bi Ryu Gang	  SLD May 11	  7,000	China</p>
<p>Dai Hong Dan	 SLD May 11	  7,000	China</p>
<p>Sin Hung 2	   N/A		  12,500	Bangladesh</p>
<p>Rio Venture	  N/A		  16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Kassos		 N/A		  16,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Hakki Uzunoglu     N/A		  10,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Jin Shan Bao	 ETD May 16	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Bong San	     ETD May 15	 12,000	Bangladesh</p>
<p>Sea Harvest	  ETA May 14	 14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Pu Cheng	     ETB May 13	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Sonamai		ETA May 26-30     1,300	Cambodia</p>
<p>Galactica	    N/A		  14,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Alam Taba	    N/A		  15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Burgos		 ETA May 17	 15,500	Japan</p>
<p>Corali		 ETA May 14-15    15,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Ots Uranus	   ETA May 13-15     6,500	Vietnam</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	 ETA May 16	 16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Huang Hua	    N/A		  13,850	Japan</p>
<p>Zangzasan Chong    ETB May 14	 10,000	Sri Lanka</p>
<p>Chong Chon Gang    ETA May 13	 12,000	Pakistan</p>
<p>Asian Spirit	 ETA May 10-20     8,000	Japan</p>
<p>Sea Hog		ETA May 16	  5,000	Mozambique</p>
<p>Alam Teguh	   ETA May 22	 15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangkhonthi	  ETA May 22	  6,000	Singapore</p>
<p>Hei Hu Quan	  ETA May 18	 14,700	South Korea</p>
<p>Nongkai Navee	ETA May 13	 12,000	Japan</p>
<p>EGN I		  ETA May 15-16     1,100	Singapore</p>
<p>Orient Express I   ETA May 16-17     1,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
